The keyboard's In-keyboard dictation (targets/CodictateDictationKeyboard:
KeyboardWebCapture.swift, KeyboardParakeet.swift, InKeyboardDictation.swift)
adapts code from two projects under the MIT License:

- Hex (https://github.com/anomalyco/hex), Copyright (c) 2026 Christopher
  Langton: the WebKit microphone capture page and WAV writer, Parakeet loading
  in the keyboard with its Neural Engine check and memory budget, and the
  resume request for audio the capture interrupted.
- ios-keyboard-dictation (https://github.com/stephancill/ios-keyboard-dictation),
  Copyright (c) 2026 Stephan Cilliers: the native heartbeat and page watchdog
  that stop the microphone when the keyboard stops pinging.

The Dictation AU (targets/CodictateFormattingAU: DictationAU.swift,
DictationAUMessageChannel.swift, DictationAUContract.swift) and its keyboard client
(targets/CodictateDictationKeyboard/KeyboardDictationAUClient.swift) adapt source
code from KeyVox (https://github.com/macmixing/keyvox), Copyright (c) 2026
Dominic Esposito, under the MIT License: hosting an out-of-process Audio Unit
extension from a keyboard and exchanging messages with it over AUMessageChannel.
Only MIT-licensed source code is used; none of KeyVox's excluded assets or branding.

